@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@
+# Fengjia: one market-entry proposal
+
+The proposal uses the **actual wavy rainbow street-entry sign**, with four yellow
+stars and two white circular end panels, above compact modern shopfronts and
+practical awnings. This is visible in photograph `1X3A9879` from the
+[official municipal film location gallery](https://filmtaichung.org.tw/scenesContent/113).
+The gallery's other street views establish close-set counters, projecting sign
+boxes and repeated fabric/metal canopies. Its separate Fun Star commercial gate
+is not the model for this asset.
+
+Fengjia is a shopping-and-food street district around Wenhua Road, rather than
+one monumental building. The
+[official Taichung Tourism page](https://travel.taichung.gov.tw/zh-tw/attractions/intro/39)
+places it by the university and extending toward Fuxing Road. The game proposal
+compresses that district into a short entry scene. Its central dark market-lane
+mouth is a **game adaptation for a future gym entrance**, not a surveyed building
+door. Adjacent frontage proportions are representative, not a parcel-by-parcel
+reconstruction. The reference photographs have no supplied capture dates.
+
+Preserve the rainbow banner's shallow curve, four-star rhythm, round end panels,
+awning profiles and narrow storefront rhythm when reducing to native size.
+Simplify window grids, merchandise and metal supports. Keep commercial lettering
+and logos absent; the study leaves blank sign bands for later hand-authored
+localization. Bright sign faces do not imply a citywide nighttime lighting mode.
+
+The single built-in imagegen result is saved unchanged at
+`artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/landmark-art/fengjia-study-v1.png` relative to
+the project root. Two official photographs guided the architecture/materials;
+the approved native Station sprite guided pixel treatment only. Exact prompt,
+photo URLs, source hashes, input roles and tool mode are recorded beside this
+brief. No correction generation was needed for the first architecture review.
+
+The image is1536×1024, the requested nominal192×128 at8×, but is a **study**:
+its76,104 visible RGB colors, soft alpha/glow and nonuniform8×8 blocks do not meet
+native format constraints. Alpha ranges0..254, with721,070 partially transparent
+pixels. The useful alpha224 silhouette bounds are(74,283)..(1455,883), exclusive.
+The built-in preview shows the complete asset; local `view_image` renders the
+soft-alpha original mostly blank. Recorded pixel samples and identical copy
+hashes confirm the preserved file. No alpha repair or creative raster edit was
+performed.
+
+Keep the existing Xitun entrance(24,12), approach(24,13) and arrival(24,15) as
+future integration constraints. The nominal12×8-metatile image request is not an
+approved map footprint. Origin, collision, portal binding, palette and shared
+Xitun bank allocation remain unassigned. `nativeReady=false`.
+
+The user approved this architecture direction with **“Use this direction”**.
+The approved high-resolution original remains unchanged. A bounded native format
+conversion is now prepared in this leaf; it creates no map or bank allocation.
+
+`candidate-maxcoverage/candidate-indexed.png` is the recommended format input for
+Root's integration review:160×96, hard alpha224, coherent2-pixel clusters,
+15 opaque GBA colors,134 unmerged graphics (144 padded). The palette preserves
+the blue/cyan/green/yellow banner, red awnings, both white end panels and four
+separate yellow star components. The tiny stars are4–6 pixels wide and4 pixels
+high; exact points are simplified. `candidate-192/` provides the requested
+unregistered192×128 alternative with larger4–6-pixel-high yellow components,
+at186 graphics (192 padded). The first median-palette160×96 conversion remains
+in `candidate/`; it muted the blue/cyan and is not the recommended input.
+
+All three variants pass binary alpha,2-pixel grid, flip-aware4bpp, CRLF/BGR555
+palette, native `gbagfx` equivalence and ten-file deterministic rebuild checks.
+These are unmerged format costs, not a claim that either candidate fits the
+combined Xitun bank. Candidate palette9 is unallocated.
+
+The entrance needs an explicit integration decision. In the160×96 candidate,
+the central lane ROI(68,62)..(92,96) has48 alpha0 pixels in only its first two
+rows, and768 opaque pixels below. It is not an alpha0 corridor. The hypothetical
+local(5,5) cell is256/256 opaque pixels of dark RGB(24,24,40), with no painted
+door frame or leaf. Both inspected shopfront regions are open counters and
+supports, with no distinct painted gym door. Nothing was erased or drawn by
+conversion to change that fact.
+
+Root's potential origin(19,7) would align local(5,5) to world(24,12), but it is
+not an approved placement or portal. A floating wooden General door in the lane
+has not been approved. Root must choose a plausible entry treatment, collision
+and shared-bank allocation, while retaining the fixed door/approach/arrival
+contract. Measurements and these boundaries are in `entrance-analysis.json`
+and `native-candidate.json`. `nativeReady=false` until installation and runtime
+checks pass.
