+# Maple Garden: one park-module proposal
+
+The landmark identity is the sunken pond and curved green embankments, with pale winding paths and the red-railed crossing bridge. The official district photo also clearly shows a low glazed park-side facility beneath a thin angled concrete canopy with inclined supports. It is a secondary element on the near/left rim, not a stand-alone generic gym. Its current tenant/use is not asserted.
+
+The proposed north-up GBA module will compress those observed elements into one daylight park sprite: a lowered basin, asymmetric pond, curved lawns/paths, one red-railed crossing and the actual modern pavilion. Omit skyline, people, temporary banners, logos and invented architecture. Do not borrow Taichung Park’s twin traditional pavilions. The boundary should blend as an ordinary terrain module, not a floating fantasy island.
+
+Two downloaded official photographs were viewed before generation; exact URLs, dimensions and SHA-256 hashes are in `references-v1.json`: [Tourism pond overview](https://travel.taichung.gov.tw/en/attractions/intro/851), [Xitun District facility/bridge photo](https://www.xitun.taichung.gov.tw/831932/831997/1513668/1514036).
+
+The supplied landscape priority plus the clear facility photo resolve the study focus without an additional pre-generation question. This is a composition proposal; the park geometry and facility position are compressed/authored, not a surveyed site plan. Final silhouette, footprint and palette still require review. Door12,32, approach12,33 and arrival12,35 remain unchanged for Main’s later binding. No native map, bank, C or save data is edited.
