@@ -0,0 +1,142 @@
+# Miyahara architectural study
+
+Create one recognizable south-facing Miyahara cutout for the same north-up GBA
+overworld treatment as the approved Old Station and National Taichung Theater.
+The user approved the architectural direction with “Use this direction”. The
+original study activates no gym warp, collision, tile palette or native asset.
+
+## Reference hierarchy
+
+The official owner's complete exterior photograph is the architecture source:
+`artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/landmark-references/miyahara-official-owner-front.jpg`.
+It shows the building's two historic brick levels, long arcade wing, narrower
+return, pale corner portal and substantial modern glass enclosure above them.
+The original dark evening exposure supplies geometry, not a night-lighting brief.
+
+The accepted native Station and Theater rasters supply pixel treatment, restrained
+material colors, horizontal facade projection and visible roof depth only. Their
+clocks, towers, theater curves and overall building geometry must not transfer.
+The tourism page's downloaded hero photograph was inspected and found to show
+the interior. It is recorded as unused context, not an exterior input.
+
+## Recognizable features, in order
+
+1. The dark faceted glass upper enclosure with thin diagonal diamond framing.
+2. Preserved red-brick walls and the rhythm of dark arched ground-floor openings.
+3. Narrow rectangular upper-story windows beneath pale cornice lines.
+4. The pale stone portal around the chamfered corner entry.
+5. A longer left brick wing and shorter right return, compressed for the game.
+
+Keep the flat roof plane visible behind the sloping glass faces. Rooftop equipment
+is subordinate and should remain simple. The building must not become a red-tile
+roofed generic shop, symmetrical courthouse or clock-tower station. The printed
+roof name, commercial signs, surrounding blocks, trees, vehicles and people are
+omitted. No text, UI, ground tile or watermark belongs in this asset.
+
+## Rendering and materials
+
+Use flat coherent pixel clusters, economical brick texture and dark readable
+outlines. Warm terracotta and red-brown brick contrast with pale cream stone,
+charcoal/slate-blue glass and restrained cool highlights. These are material
+families, not a registered native palette. The eventual raster must use binary
+alpha, at most 15 opaque colors per 8×8 graphic and flip-aware deduplication.
+
+The intended envelope is provisionally 160×128 logical pixels, 10×8 metatiles.
+The requested first canvas was 1280×1024 at integer scale8. The actual built-in
+output is 1402×1122, with soft alpha and many more colors than a native bank can
+use. Its measured pixel-grid and palette failures are explicit in
+`measurements.json`; this preserved original is a study, not a source tilesheet.
+
+## Entrance and map contracts
+
+The current native door stays (20,52) in `MAP_TAICHUNG_OLD_CITY`, exterior warp2.
+The approach remains (20,53), safe arrival (20,55), and the three gym return warps
+remain unchanged. A proposed 10×8 art envelope at origin (15,45) would keep the
+active door at local (5,7), with opening columns4–5. It is unregistered and not a
+collision reservation. Its larger area overlaps part of the existing western
+street and northeastern grove; actual alpha and geometry must be checked before
+placement.
+
+The separate v2 pilot proposes rectangle [21,38,30,45], entrance (26,45), arrival
+(26,48). These are authored pilot-local coordinates. They do not replace native
+map or warp coordinates.
+
+The original generated portal is visibly right of the intended target column if
+the body fills all 160 pixels. The encoded candidate instead fits the entire
+building into 128 pixels at the left of the 160-pixel canvas, preserving its mass
+and leaving a 32-pixel right buffer. The measured glass-door span x80..93,y116..123
+then fits local cell (5,7), so the existing global warp need not move. Painted
+pixels still require an actual native door binding. Collision remains separate
+from alpha; approach and arrival must stay clear.
+
+## Budget and acceptance
+
+The observed current OldCity Station compiler has 289 unique secondary graphics,
+304 loaded sheet slots, Station palette7 and a shared accent reservation at12.
+This snapshot is not an allocation for Miyahara. Ordinary-building color families
+and other landmarks may consume the same bank. Root must recount the actual
+scene, graphics and palette union when converting this study; no inherited roof
+budget is assumed.
+
+The independent encoded candidate passes exact logical size, entry alignment,
+binary alpha, exact Station palette7 and native format round-trip checks. It
+costs 146 unique graphics before any shared-bank merge, with 40 occupied metatile
+cells. That cost cannot simply be added to Station's 289 within the 384 limit. Root
+owns the combined graphics/palette allocation; this is not a separate full bank.
+Source ground composition, collision/road clearance, fixed-door animation and
+three return-warp checks in a running ROM remain. `nativeReady` stays false.
+
+## Generation provenance
+
+One built-in `image_gen` reference-guided generation produced
+`artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/landmark-art/miyahara-study-v1.png`.
+It is an unchanged copy of the built-in output. The separate `candidate/` files
+are deterministic mechanical conversion, not another creative generation.
+`generation-prompt.txt` is the exact built-in prompt;
+`generation.json` records mode, inputs, output hashes and review state.
+
+Official sources: [Miyahara owner website](https://www.miyahara.com.tw/) and
+[Taichung Tourism's Miyahara page](https://travel.taichung.gov.tw/en/attractions/intro/1239).
+Photographs remain isolated reference-only downloads outside versioned native art.
+
+## Encoded candidate limits
+
+The 128×76 body sits at (0,52) in the 160×128 canvas. Its 2×2 native pixel clusters
+simplify the fine glass diamonds and brick texture. A larger body would improve
+those small details but increase graphics cost and alter the fixed-entry fit;
+V1 is preserved and the one subsequent quality trial is described below. The whole body remains visible,
+without a horizontal squash, clipped wing or mirrored facade.
+
+All 80 envelope cells have foreground references, 40 contain ink, and 41 foreground
+definitions are distinct including the empty definition. A 128-pixel-wide tile
+sheet pads the 146 unique graphics to 160 slots. `tiles.4bpp` contains 146 unpadded
+graphics for the Root merger; its relative tilemap must not be treated as a
+640-based registered map. Palette 7 uses the exact 16-entry Station palette, with
+15 available opaque colors and no new color or palette bank.
+
+The first three metatile rows and last two columns are transparent. The northern
+grove is therefore outside the ink, but the western edge still reaches native
+street column 15 at rows48..52. Root must compose against the actual baseline and
+erase the complete old placeholder, including its column 23 inside the right
+buffer, before overlaying this candidate.
+
+## V2 native-pixel quality trial
+
+Root authorized one trial to recover the diamond lattice lost in V1's 2×2 sampling.
+The separate V2 encoder uses BOX downsampling at one native pixel and nearest
+assignment to the unchanged Station palette, with no dithering. It retains the
+same 160×128 canvas and 128×76 body at (0,52). The source study and all V1 assets are
+preserved; no additional image generation was performed.
+
+V2 costs 152 unique graphics rather than 146. Both sheets pad to 160 slots, so this
+quality improvement adds no loaded sheet row. It keeps 40 occupied cells and 41
+distinct foreground definitions. Connected roof cross-braces are clearer, and
+V2 is recommended for the next integration trial, subject to Root's combined
+allocation. It is not a separate full bank.
+
+Its measured door glass is x79..94,y116..123, centered at (86.5,119.5), unchanged
+from V1's center. One glass-border pixel falls left of the target cell; record
+that when composing the actual animated door rather than moving the fixed warp.
+The V2 checker passes native formats, exact shared palette, binary alpha,
+deterministic regeneration, actual gbagfx and preservation of 14 V1/source hashes.
+The separate `native-candidate-v2.json` contains the full measurements.
