+Use case: stylized-concept.
+Asset type: one proposed original landmark building cutout for a north-up Game Boy Advance / FireRed city, to be mechanically encoded into native tiles after review.
+
+Input image 1 is the official photograph of the NATIONAL MUSEUM OF NATURAL SCIENCE main exhibition entrance in Taichung. This is the architecture reference and the user specifically chose this entrance. Input image 2 is the actual approved native Station sprite: use ONLY its north-up frontal RPG projection, pixel scale, palette restraint and visible roof depth. Do not copy its clock, brick, towers or roof shape.
+
+Create one recognizable low, wide, gray modern exhibition building. Follow image1's broad rectilinear concrete/stone blocks; the taller central projecting rectangular entry bay contains a very deep dark entrance recess with two thin pale columns/supports and glass doors set back. Use long dark horizontal window bands on both low wings, with the modest stepped flat-roof blocks visible behind. Preserve the nearly symmetrical wide front and the clear deeply recessed portal. The photo's cyan temporary exhibition banner is omitted, leaving gray wall above the portal. Include only building fabric, including its real understated roof volumes; no distant skyscrapers, trees, courtyard, banners or greenhouse. This must not become the Botanical Garden glasshouse, a generic classical museum, an elaborate atrium, a white temple, a stadium or a civic palace.
+
+Projection: south-facing facade horizontal, north-up orthographic RPG view, modest roof surfaces visible from above, vertical walls vertical, no diagonal isometric rotation or camera vanishing point. One complete centered building, uncropped on true transparency. Target logical envelope 192x128 game pixels, 12x8 metatiles; if enlarged output use consistent 8x8 hard pixel clusters on a1536x1024 canvas. The building is intentionally broad and low and can occupy only the bottom80–96 logical pixels. Keep the main doorway at the center of bottom metatile row7, future active doorway in column6. No drawn grid or coordinate labels.
+
+Pixel treatment: flat, economical, crisp GBA pixel clusters matching image2; broad repeatable stone bands and window modules rather than noisy tiny texture. About14 opaque shades total, warm light gray, cool medium gray, charcoal recess, muted blue-gray glass and ivory columns. Uniform hard square pixel clusters, opaque structural edges, binary alpha, very small upper-left material highlights. Preserve simple gray material identity rather than adding bright saturated facade colors.
+
+Outside the building must be true transparent alpha. No ground plane, paving, grass, people, landscaping, cars, scooters, steps extending across a courtyard, text, logo, lettering, labels, interface, watermark, checkerboard background, shadows outside the building, gradients, bloom, antialiasing, painterly texture or photographic material noise. Return only the proposed building sprite.
