+# Shen Ji: first proposed architecture study
+
+The built-in imagegen proposal is saved unchanged at
+`artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/landmark-art/shen-ji-study-v1.png` relative to the
+project root. It shows two cream dormitories, red/orange roofs, a narrow lane,
+an attached stair and a clear ground-floor entry on the left building.
+
+The user approved the two-dormitory direction with **“Use this direction”**.
+The original image remains unchanged as the architecture master.
+
+The two official tourism photographs were downloaded and hash-matched to the
+previously inspected references, then inspected locally. The archived approved
+Station study was used for pixel treatment only. Its architecture was not a
+source for these dormitories. Exact inputs and attribution are in `references.json`;
+the exact built-in prompt is `generation-prompt-v1.txt`.
+
+The output is 1536×1024, corresponding to the requested nominal 192×128 at 8×.
+It retains soft alpha/glow, 95,490 visible RGBA values and no uniform complete
+aligned 8×8 logical blocks. It is a study rather than a native source raster.
+The continuous gap at alpha 224 is 20 source pixels, about 2.5 nominal pixels; it
+is not a verified walkable game lane. Native footprint and gap width need review.
+
+Keep the current Greenway door (10,44), approach (10,45) and arrival (10,47). No map
+envelope, collision, palette, bank or door behavior is allocated by this image.
+Root owns those later decisions. A separate bounded native format conversion is
+now available; no creative code redraw, map installation or second generation
+was performed. `nativeReady=false` until integration and runtime checks.
+
+The first indexed candidate is160×96 with142 unique graphics and13 used opaque
+GBA colors in candidate palette9. Its15,360 pixels round-trip through4bpp/flips;
+CRLF palette encoding, BGR555, deterministic output and actual gbagfx checks pass.
+Source alpha224 has exactly two clean components; their boxes and membership
+proof are recorded without changing the source study.
+
+Root then approved an exact game-map module layout: left80×96 at(0,0), right96×96
+at(96,0), on a192×96 canvas. All original opaque indices are conserved; the right
+building moves24 pixels and adds zero8×8 patterns. The localx80..95 lane is fully
+transparent. At Root's origin(7,39), it is global column12; the left door remains
+local(3,5), global(10,44). The old placeholder must be restored under the lane
+before the game can treat it as walkable. No native map was written.
+
+The exact192×96 layout reaches global column18 at that origin, where Root
+identified protected tall grass. Keep it unchanged as the exact-conservation
+V1 alternative. It is not the current map-fit proposal.
+
+Root requested one mechanical V2 city-fit alternative. Its left opaque70×66
+crop is nearest-sampled to30×28, enlarged to60×56 in2-pixel clusters, and placed
+at(4,40) on a64×96 module. The right96×96 module remains pixel-exact, placed
+at(80,0) on a176×96 canvas. No new color, architecture or image generation was
+introduced. This resize preserves the subject's aspect ratio within1.1% rounding;
+it does not conserve every original left-building pixel. The original study,
+160×96 indexed source, modules and exact192×96 V1 remain byte-identical.
+
+Use `candidate/nativecourtyard-layout-v2-indexed.png` and its companion JSON for
+the current Root-requested integration proposal. It has125 unmerged graphics
+(128 padded),39 occupied metatiles and40 distinct foreground definitions. All
+16,896 pixels round-trip through4bpp and flip references; seven V2 outputs
+rebuild byte-identically. The measured doorway panel is(46,84)..(53,93), centered
+at(49.5,88.5): local(3,5), preserving global(10,44). The localx64..79 lane is
+fully transparent, corresponding to global column11; no ink reaches column18.
+Actual collision, terrain restoration, shared Greenway allocation and runtime
+checks remain Root's integration work. `nativeReady=false`.
