+# Unmerged Park native candidate
+
+The approved pavilion study has one mechanical native-size candidate:
+`candidate/candidate-native.png` at 192×128 pixels. Its 4× nearest-neighbor review
+image is `artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/landmark-art/park-native-candidate-v1.png`.
+The source study is unchanged. No new image generation or creative repair was
+performed.
+
+The pipeline thresholds the source alpha at 224, crops the retained silhouette,
+fits the complete body to 176×96 pixels and places it at `(16,32)` on the logical
+canvas. Premultiplied RGBA BOX resampling retains one-native-pixel detail; nearest
+RGB assignment uses only the exact Station palette's opaque indices 1–15, with
+no dithering. Final alpha is binary after a coverage threshold of 128. The palette
+constraint shifts some roof tones toward the Station's available slate/olive
+colors; there are no added Park colors or palette banks.
+
+## Measured cost before any bank merge
+
+| Item | Count |
+| --- | ---: |
+| Unique 8×8 graphics, including the transparent graphic | 185 |
+| Graphics sheet slots after row padding | 192 |
+| 8×8 tilemap placements | 384 |
+| Foreground metatile cells in the 12×8 canvas | 96 |
+| Occupied foreground cells | 52 |
+| Distinct four-word foreground definitions | 53 |
+| New colors / additional palette banks | 0 / 0 |
+
+These are isolated candidate costs. They exclude the Station, Miyahara, ordinary
+city art and ground. No assertion is made that the combined city fits a
+384-graphic secondary bank. Root owns the combined primary/secondary graphics and
+metatile audit. Tile entries use relative candidate graphic indices and palette
+7; they must be remapped before any actual bank composition. Four-word
+foreground definitions are art quadrants, not complete native ground/attribute
+definitions.
+
+## The painted approach remains blocked
+
+The requested local door cell is `(6,7)`, pixel rectangle `[96,112,111,127]`,
+center `(104,120)`. Proposed baseline origin `(26,23)` plus that local cell equals
+the existing Park door `(32,30)`. The existing approach `(32,31)` and arrival
+`(32,34)` are not changed here.
+
+The red stub's measured source-color extent projects to `[92,109,115,126]`,
+crossing local columns 5–7 and rows 6–7. Its projected color mask overlaps 121
+pixels of the intended door cell. The center `(104,120)` itself is red palette
+index 7. The inspected dark/glazing extent above the barrier is
+`[96,100,111,113]`, centered at `(103.5,106.5)`. It is not a verified open portal.
+
+The shared palette also maps neighboring brown timber to red-family indices.
+That broader palette-color extent, `[88,108,120,126]`, is reported separately in
+the manifest. Color masks measure the painted image; they do not establish
+walkability or collision. Root can replace the functional door cell during
+composition. No ground, bridge correction, collision, active warp or return was
+invented in this candidate.
+
+## Files and checks
+
+`candidate/` contains the indexed and RGBA images, indexed tile sheet, packed
+4bpp graphics, relative tilemap/foreground definitions, a copy of palette 7 and
+the manifests. `07.pal` is written as CRLF bytes from the start, matching the
+repository's checkout convention; its recorded SHA256 hashes that representation.
+
+```sh
+/Users/peter/.pyenv/versions/3.11.15/bin/python3 -B \
+  data/taichung/landmarks/taichung-park/encode_candidate.py
+/Users/peter/.pyenv/versions/3.11.15/bin/python3 -B \
+  data/taichung/landmarks/taichung-park/check_candidate.py
+```
+
+Checks decode the actual packed files and reconstruct the native PNG, verify
+flip flags, foreground definitions, palette/GBA bytes and canonical CRLF,
+compare the source and palette hashes, and confirm the barrier still covers the
+intended entry. `candidate/validation.json` records the result.
+
+The candidate remains `nativeReady=false`, unmerged and unregistered. No C,
+shared bank, map, welcome-room source or geometry contract was edited.
