+Use case: stylized-concept.
+Asset type: one original pixel-art overworld landmark cutout for a FireRed-style Taichung game; an architectural study awaiting native tile encoding.
+
+Input image1 is an official elevated nighttime exterior of NATIONAL TAICHUNG THEATER. Use it for the building's full massing and actual facade arrangement. Input image2 is an official daylight close exterior view: use it for the pale concrete, curved recesses, blue-gray glass and thin dark glazing grid. Reinterpret the full building in neutral daylight, without the city, road, fountain or nighttime glow. Input image3 is the approved Old Taichung Station pixel-art study: use ONLY its crisp stepped pixel clusters and restrained game-art finish, not its architecture or materials. Input image4 is a native FireRed screenshot: use ONLY its north-up overworld roof/facade perspective and game readability, not its generic museum geometry, colors or surroundings.
+
+Draw the recognizable NATIONAL TAICHUNG THEATER designed by Toyo Ito: a broad low-rise rectangular modern building with a mostly straight flat roof boundary, light ivory concrete surfaces that swell inward and outward into organic bottle/hourglass profiles, large irregular curved openings and recessed sound-cave forms, and monumental blue-gray glazed areas with a fine dark window grid. Preserve the irregular facade rhythm visible in the exterior reference, including a large central pinched glass field and curved side openings; avoid a generic row of identical arches. Show just enough roof/top depth to read as an overworld building. Simplify its tiny breathing-hole dots to a few small accents. No brick, pitched roof, clock, tower, dome, castle details, columns, giant theatrical masks or invented ornament.
+
+The facade faces south, remains horizontal and centered, and the camera is the ordinary north-up RPG overworld view: see the front and some roof from above, orthographic and aligned to a square grid. No diagonal isometric rotation or photographic vanishing-point perspective. Keep the full rectangular mass uncropped. The central ground-level glass entrance is clear at the bottom center; its visual doorway spans logical metatile columns7–8 of the bottom row9, with future active entry at column8.
+
+Target a256×160 logical-pixel sprite:16×10 metatiles of16 pixels. Request a1536×960 image representing exactly6× integer enlargement, with each logical pixel a6×6 hard-edged square if possible. Use economical charcoal outlines, flat opaque pixel clusters, simple two- or three-tone shading from upper left, roughly24 opaque colors, warm white/ivory concrete, cool gray shadow, desaturated cyan/blue glass and dark blue-gray window frames. The architecture's curves must be deliberate pixel stair-steps rather than smooth vector curves or blurred shading. Keep the same pixel-art family as the approved Station study while simplifying texture further.
+
+Return ONLY this one building on a genuinely transparent background. All pixels outside its silhouette must have alpha0, and the building should be opaque with hard alpha edges. No surrounding glow, halo, fog, detached ground shadow or feathering. No people, vehicles, fountain, pools, ground, pavement, trees, garden scene, skyline, text, signage, projection patterns, labels, UI, frame, logos or watermark. No gradients, antialiasing, blur, painterly rendering, photorealism or smooth vector illustration.
