@@ -0,0 +1,225 @@
+# Native neighborhood color and fill studies
+
+This workstream adds native-index color recipes and source-composed neighborhood
+studies. It does not edit registered maps, global tileset assets, native warp
+events, existing General/PewterCity graphics or palettes, or the baseline ROM.
+The first independently reviewable item is one32×24 old-core block, followed by
+filling the separately approved64×64 geography pilot's24 candidate lots.
+
+## Shared palette12 recipe
+
+`data/taichung/prefabs/colorways.json` defines all sixteen entries exactly. Entry0
+retains transparency;1 is shared outline,2 shared highlight and15 shared concrete.
+Terracotta uses3–5, teal6–8, mustard9–11 and slate12–14. The four three-shade ramps
+coexist in the same palette bank. All RGB values are aligned to5-bit native color;
+the compiler emits both JASC-PAL and the actual BGR555 bank bytes.
+
+Source selection is specific: Pewter palette8 graphics containing roof shades at
+indices5,6,7, with no window/non-roof colors, are cloned and remapped. The selected
+graphic's neutral trim indices are mapped to shared neutrals. Metatile parts
+outside that mask retain source palette/graphics. Coloring applies only to the
+first three roof rows of eligible ordinary houses, corner stores and walk-ups.
+Façades, source-blue alternatives, red stalls and cream/stonework remain available.
+This is native tile/palette data, not a display filter.
+
+## Compiler API and allocation
+
+`tools/taichung/streetscape/color_compile.py` exports:
+
+```python
+compiled = compile_colorways(
+    source=ROOT, catalog=None, colorways=None,
+    variant_metatile_start=None,
+)
+words = color_grid(compiled, source_composition, placements)
+save_native(compiled, output_directory)
+```
+
+The returned object contains indexed64-pixel `graphics` tiles, `metatiles` with
+global graphics IDs/flip/palette bits, `attributes`, `palettes`, color `remaps`,
+the original `library`, the `recipe`, and a `budget` manifest. Horizontal/vertical
+flips are deduplicated and reference flags adjusted to preserve displayed pixels.
+The mapping integrator owns merging these arrays with Station graphics and native
+registration. Shared General primary graphics remain unchanged.
+
+Measured source-kit/color-only allocation:
+
+- 62 source-kit secondary graphics after flip deduplication.
+- 13 selected source roof graphics; four color families add48 graphics after dedup.
+- 110 secondary graphics total, plus131 already-shared General primary graphics.
+- 79 original secondary metatile slots preserved;32 roof variants yield111 slots.
+- Default color variant IDs0x2CF–0x2EE; pass `variant_metatile_start` to move them
+  clear of Station allocations. Native secondary IDs must remain within0x280–0x3FF.
+- Palette12 is the sole new color bank. Source kit banks8–11 remain unchanged;
+  Station bank7 is reserved by the mapping integrator's separate implementation.
+
+The source-kit count excludes extra graphics used only by current baseline maps.
+The integrator must include their actual union when assembling a whole-map bank.
+
+`save_native` emits `tiles.4bpp`, indexed `tiles.png`, `metatiles.bin`,
+`metatile_attributes.bin`, `12.pal`, `12.gbapal`, and `compile-manifest.json`.
+The PNG has row padding to a16-tile-wide sheet; the raw4bpp file and returned arrays
+contain the logical110 tiles. These are encodable integration fixtures, not assets
+already registered in the ROM.
+
+## First game-scale block
+
+`neighborhood_pilot.py` composes a32×24-tile source block using the old-core profile
+`city-v2-r2-c2`. Older low-rise runs, a taller teal walk-up and closer commercial
+frontage provide use/height/material contrast. The native Red standing sprite is
+included only as a16×32 scale reference. Native dimensions, dormant doors and
+approach masks are preserved; no new NPC/event is registered.
+
+The fixture demonstrates the profile's direction, not a measured parcel map or a
+claim to hit all authored density percentages. Roads/lots in this first small
+study are independent source composition, not the frozen64×64 pilot geometry.
+
+```sh
+/Users/peter/.pyenv/versions/3.11.15/bin/python3 -B \
+  tools/taichung/streetscape/neighborhood_pilot.py \
+  --output /Users/peter/devday_hackathon/artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/neighborhoods/old-core-pilot
+
+/Users/peter/.pyenv/versions/3.11.15/bin/python3 -B \
+  tools/taichung/streetscape/color_check.py
+```
+
+The independently checked first fixture has528 reachable cells, four reachable
+egresses and nine reachable dormant door approaches. Coloring changes no collision
+or elevation bits. All four palette12 families appear simultaneously alongside
+existing blue/red/cream source colors.
+
+`color_check.py` compares105 base-metatile renders against the original source
+renderer, all32 roof-remap renders against an independent original-pixel material
+shader,110 native4bpp graphics through a binary roundtrip,888 native16-bit metatile
+entries through a roundtrip, and all16 BGR555 palette entries through a roundtrip.
+The source-original render equivalence also verifies tile-flip packing.
+
+First review artifacts are under `artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/neighborhoods/old-core-pilot/`:
+
+- `pilot-block-overview.png`: annotated32×24 study, with exact native pixels scaled
+  by nearest neighbor.
+- `pilot-block-native.png`:512×384 source frame at native asset scale.
+- `pilot-camera-crop-240x160.png`: native-resolution camera-size crop; source study,
+  not a fabricated emulator screenshot.
+- `pilot-plan.json`, `pilot-map.bin`, `pilot-validation.json`, `color-validation.json`.
+- `native-color-bank/`: actual indexed graphics, palette and metatile encodings.
+
+The remaining broader neighborhood examples are queued after the accepted focused
+review cadence; no second/third example is needed to block delivery of this one.
+
+## Approved 64×64 lot fill and density revision
+
+`neighborhood_fill.py` creates the first complete fill of the geography pilot's
+24 frozen lots. The accepted R2C2 profile supplies use/age/material direction;
+municipal road data and the authored layout remain separate from those game
+assignments. Its V1 artifacts remain preserved in `neighborhoods/r2c2-filled/`.
+
+`neighborhood_density.py` creates one focused V2 in a separate output directory.
+It replaces small isolated commercial buildings with broader paired shop bays
+and taller mixed-use facades. Commercial aprons use smooth paving; quieter
+residential courts use stone paving and two deliberately placed rear boundaries.
+New public sidewalk paving stays outside all approved lots and gym reserves.
+This ground treatment is authored gameplay streetscape, not a surveyed land-cover
+claim. Every building and prop, including its clear apron, stays inside its lot.
+
+Three derived source-only modules are exported in the V2 artifact catalog:
+
+| Stable prefab ID | Metatile dimensions including apron | Role |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `building-mixed-use-mid` | 5×6 | Commercial glazing below homes |
+| `building-mixed-use-tall` | 5×8 | Taller homes over a shop |
+| `building-shop-row-pair` | 10×5 | Two contiguous shop bays |
+
+They recombine the existing walk-up/corner-store roofs, masonry and General
+display-window tiles. They introduce no graphics, palette entries or metatile
+variants beyond the color pack. Their art remains provisional FireRed reuse,
+with dormant entrances. The base 17-item catalog and compiler API are unchanged.
+
+Integration helpers are:
+
+```python
+catalog, added_prefab_ids = density_catalog()
+compiled = compile_density(output_directory, variant_metatile_start=None)
+result = fill_density(compiled, frozen_layout, old_core_profile)
+```
+
+`compile_density` writes the derived catalog and recipe as reviewable JSON. Its
+optional metatile start is forwarded to `compile_colorways` so the integrator can
+avoid Station allocations. The result contains native words, lot-assigned
+placements, per-lot records, protected masks and validation. Placement `lotId`
+and `colorway` are metadata; remove both before calling `Library.compose`.
+
+Generate and check the focused V2 with:
+
+```sh
+/Users/peter/.pyenv/versions/3.11.15/bin/python3 -B \
+  tools/taichung/streetscape/neighborhood_density.py \
+  --output /Users/peter/devday_hackathon/artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/neighborhoods/r2c2-filled-v2
+
+/Users/peter/.pyenv/versions/3.11.15/bin/python3 -B \
+  tools/taichung/streetscape/neighborhood_density_check.py \
+  --output /Users/peter/devday_hackathon/artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/neighborhoods/r2c2-filled-v2 \
+  --v1 /Users/peter/devday_hackathon/artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/neighborhoods/r2c2-filled
+```
+
+The V2 contains 25 building/stall modules across all 24 lots, 2 rear boundaries,
+and 27 dormant entrance reservations. Commercial lot solid coverage increases
+from 233/400 cells (58.25%) to 319/400 cells (79.75%). All 899 protected road and
+arrival-path cells, the 3 landmark south arrivals and the 6 road exits are
+reachable. The 1,098 new sidewalk cells also remain reachable. There are zero
+lot/apron overflows or road/gym-reserve collisions.
+
+`neighborhood_density_check.py` checks all 1,311 road/gym-reserve/approach cells
+byte-for-byte against V1; it also records and verifies hashes of every V1 artifact.
+Repeated composition is deterministic. Derived catalog graphic/metatile arrays
+are exactly equal to the original color pack, so the independent source-render
+and roof-shader checks cover them. The saved V2 files separately roundtrip all
+110 4bpp graphics, 888 metatile references and 16 BGR555 colors. The accepted
+source-layout hash remains
+`a0f0468c6825e7132244ed13fc6ec94b66e4682e4327a32740cb7b4c38aea82d`.
+
+Review artifacts under `artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/neighborhoods/r2c2-filled-v2/`:
+
+- `filled-block-overview.png`: annotated 64×64 layout with reserved gym envelopes.
+- `filled-block-native.png`: 1024×1024 at native asset scale, with the source Red
+  standing sprite at the Station arrival as a scale reference.
+- `density-detail-32x24.png`: native-pixel crop of the west retail/residential edge.
+- `density-catalog.json`, `density-colorways.json`, `placements.json`, `filled-map.bin`.
+- `validation.json`, `density-checks.json`, `native-color-bank/`.
+- `provenance.json`: SHA-256 hashes of source scripts, recipes, source tile banks,
+  frozen geometry/profile inputs and the emitted V2 fixture files. V1 hashes are
+  separately recorded in `density-checks.json`.
+
+This ends the focused density pass. It does not compose all sixteen city sections
+or register any map, collision data, event, warp or tileset in the ROM.
+
+## Continuous city blocks
+
+`neighborhood_blocks.py` composes the old-core section as attached building rows
+over the available authored land. The original24 lots remain provenance records;
+they no longer limit the new block footprints. Stepped roof groups, residential
+floors, retail glazing and narrow public alleys provide the city fabric. All new
+block footprints are authored game geometry, not surveyed parcels.
+
+V4 has1706 building cells across2785 unreserved cells:61.26%, or68.05% after
+explicit entrance aprons. All1311 reserved road/gym/approach cells remain byte-
+identical to the earlier compositions. All three gym arrivals, six road exits
+and56 dormant entrance approaches connect to the walking network. The normal
+building bank still uses110 graphics and111 metatiles; no new graphic patterns
+were added for the larger block composition.
+
+```sh
+python3 -B tools/taichung/streetscape/neighborhood_blocks.py --output /tmp/taichung-blocks-v4
+python3 -B tools/taichung/streetscape/neighborhood_blocks_check.py --output /tmp/taichung-blocks-v4
+```
+
+Use repeated `--previous DIRECTORY` arguments with the checker to verify earlier
+V1/V2/V3 artifact preservation and invariant-cell equality. The first reviewed
+V4 output is at `artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/neighborhoods/r2c2-filled-v4/`;
+its map SHA256 is`da6aae23247a779788bfb2d75b36438829d2e841e0900e072ff1ea82c35a67ce`.
+The checker also compares107 original source renders,32 roof-shader renders,
+native binary encodings, and32 roof renders after relocating their metatile IDs.
+
+This is a source-native blockout shown for density review. Taiwan-specific
+facades, the three landmark assets and native map registration remain separate
+integration work. The registered playable districts are not replaced by V4.
