+# Miyahara first landmark study
+
+The Miyahara stream prepares one official-photo-referenced architecture study in
+parallel with the Park and ordinary neighborhood fill. Root owns the architecture
+review and any subsequent native integration. The completed Theater package is
+frozen and unchanged by this stream.
+
+## Delivered item
+
+The first built-in imagegen study is saved unchanged as
+`artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/landmark-art/miyahara-study-v1.png` and was sent to
+Root immediately when ready, before the metadata was finished. The user approved
+the brick corner arcade and diamond-glass roof with “Use this direction”. One
+bounded native encoding candidate now follows that approved architecture.
+
+The new `data/taichung/landmarks/miyahara/` package contains the exact prompt,
+official reference URLs/hashes, input roles, art brief, placement contracts,
+measured output and generation/review state. The official owner's photograph
+guides architecture. Accepted native Station and Theater images guide pixel
+treatment only. The tourism hero photograph is an interior and was not used as
+an exterior reference.
+
+## Current limits
+
+The provisional target is 160×128 logical pixels in a 10×8-metatile envelope.
+The generated canvas is 1402×1122. It has 751,972 fully transparent pixels but
+nonbinary alpha, 113,447 distinct visible RGBA values and no uniform complete
+aligned 8×8 blocks. It is an architectural study, not a native tilesheet.
+
+The original portal is right of target local column 5 when the body fills the
+canvas. The separate native candidate resolves this by fitting the complete body
+to 128 pixels wide within the 160-pixel canvas. Shared budget and map/runtime
+integration remain unapproved. `nativeReady=false`.
+
+## Coordinate separation
+
+| Contract | Door | Clear approach | Arrival | Proposed art envelope |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Current native OldCity | (20,52), warp2 | (20,53) | (20,55) | [15,45,24,52], unreviewed |
+| Separate v2 authored pilot | (26,45) | within pilot apron | (26,48) | [21,38,30,45], unregistered |
+
+The native contract comes from `docs/taichung-city-contract.json`. The separate
+pilot reserve comes from `data/taichung/neighborhoods/pilot-r2c2-layout.json`.
+Neither map, C registry, warp event nor existing landmark file was edited.
+
+## Independent encoded candidate
+
+`candidate/` contains an exact 160×128 indexed source, binary-alpha PNG, relative
+4bpp graphics/foreground references, Station palette 7 and measured manifests.
+`landmark-art/miyahara-native-candidate-v1.png` is an unchanged 4× nearest preview.
+The source study remains untouched. No second creative generation was used.
+
+The body is 128×76 at (0,52), with 32 transparent pixels at the right. It preserves
+aspect ratio and the asymmetric wings. The measured glass entry box is
+x80..93,y116..123, entirely inside local door cell (5,7); its center differs from
+target (88,120) by only (-1.5,-0.5) pixels. Native origin (15,45) therefore keeps the
+existing global door (20,52).
+
+The candidate uses the exact Station palette's 15 opaque colors, introducing zero
+colors and zero palette banks. Before any merge it costs 146 unique graphics,
+160 padded sheet slots, 40 occupied metatiles and 41 distinct foreground definitions
+including empty; the full envelope has 80 cells. Root must reconcile this cost
+with Station, Park and neighborhood color families. It does not independently
+fit in Station's remaining 95 unique slots, and no separate full bank is assumed.
+
+`check_candidate.py` passes all 20,480 pixels through 4bpp/flips, 5,120 uniform 2×2
+clusters, exact shared palette, binary alpha, doorway fit, reproducible output
+and real gbagfx sheet/palette agreement. Fine roof lattice and brick texture are
+simpler at this scale. Enlarging the body would add graphics cost and change
+entry alignment. A subsequent authorized quality trial is recorded separately below.
+
+Ink occupies only the bottom five rows and left eight columns. Root still needs
+to resolve the west street edge, restore the complete old placeholder under the
+transparent right buffer, compose native ground/collision, register the asset and
+test door animation/returns and player layering. Alpha occupancy is not collision.
+
+## One-pixel quality trial, V2
+
+Root requested one bounded trial after inspecting the V1 roof lattice. V1's
+2×2 sampling broke thin cross-braces into dots. V2 reduces the same source with
+BOX at native pixel resolution, then assigns the exact Station palette without
+dithering. Source alpha is first thresholded at224; reduced alpha is thresholded
