+# Taichung Park pavilion study
+
+One first Lake Heart Twin Pavilions study is ready at
+`artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/landmark-art/park-study-v1.png`. It was generated
+with the built-in `image_gen` tool from locally inspected official photographs,
+with the accepted Station finish and native overworld perspective as separate
+style references. It is an architecture cutout, not a lake or park scene.
+
+The user approved this architecture direction with “Use this direction.” The PNG
+is now frozen. Native encoding is deferred to Root's shared graphics-budget audit;
+the technical limitations below remain recorded and `nativeReady` remains false.
+
+The real pavilion has paired sharp, curved roof peaks, eyebrow vents, pale
+splayed columns and timber glazing around a lower connecting hall. The 2023
+restored elevation provides the gray-green metal roof color used in this study.
+Source: [official restored elevation and completion report](https://www.culture.taichung.gov.tw/2372994/post).
+
+The historic-plan description identifies two rotated-square pavilion units with
+a rectangular connector. The city also describes the curved roof geometry and
+the wooden Zhongshan Bridge's straight balusters and spindle-like posts. The
+pale masonry arched bridge visible behind some photographs is not the red wooden
+access bridge. Sources: [national heritage record](https://nchdb.boch.gov.tw/assets/overview/monument/19990417000001),
+[official roof and bridge description](https://www.culture.taichung.gov.tw/2061063/2098033/2135761),
+[municipal heritage photo gallery](https://www.tchac.taichung.gov.tw/building?pid=15&uid=33).
+
+The study shows the separate roof peaks and vents, splayed supports, timber
+windows and low hall in a frontal, north-up game camera. The small red approach
+stub is an authored abstraction rather than a geographically exact bridge
+alignment. It currently reads as a front railing blocking the entry, so it is
+not accepted as a walkable approach. Native composition should supply an open
+lane between the bridge's side railings.
+
+## Art and technical status
+
+The provisional logical target is 192×128 pixels, or 12×8 metatiles. The requested
+8× raster size of 1536×1024 pixels was met. The actual generated alpha and pixel
+grid remain unsuitable for direct native use:
+
+- 865,075 pixels are fully transparent; 707,789 have partial alpha.
+- Maximum alpha is 254, with no fully opaque pixels and 255 distinct alpha levels.
+- There are 84,672 distinct visible RGBA values, exceeding the 24-color art target.
+- None of the 13,088 visible aligned 8×8 blocks is uniform.
+- A soft halo remains around the architecture.
+
+These measurements are recorded, not repaired with an untracked image edit.
+The copied PNG is byte-for-byte identical to the built-in output. The asset
+remains `nativeReady=false`; palette assignment, tile packing, collision,
+foreground/roof layering and runtime checks are still required. Root owns the
+shared bank budget and native integration.
+
+## Coordinates stay separate
+
+`placement.json` verifies the live contract's Park baseline without changing it:
+
+| Contract | Door | Approach / arrival | Additional context |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Current native `MAP_TAICHUNG_OLD_CITY` | `(32,30)`, exterior warp 1 | approach `(32,31)`; arrival `(32,34)` | gym `MAP_TAICHUNG_PARK_GYM`; existing interior returns retained |
+| Approved R2C2 pilot, local coordinates | `(43,24)` | arrival `(43,27)` | art rectangle `[35,13,50,24]`, inclusive; reserve includes the south apron |
+
+The pilot is a new authored 64×64 section with world origin `(128,128)`. Its
+coordinates are not native map 43 coordinates. The 12×8 art target can fit inside
+the 16×12 pilot art envelope, but no final crop, origin or native entry cell is
+selected here. Generated margins and a lower-center drawn door do not establish
+a valid metatile anchor. No current map, frozen pilot, profile, warp or registry
+was changed.
+
+## Reproducible record
+
+The isolated source pack is
+`data/taichung/landmarks/taichung-park/`:
+
+- `generation-prompt-v1.txt`: exact prompt used for the single built-in call.
+- `references.json`: source URLs, reference roles, local inspections and hashes.
+- `generation.json`: requested target, output hash, visual findings and gates.
+- `study-v1-raster-check.json`: measured alpha, colors and enlarged-grid checks.
+- `placement.json`: unchanged native baseline and separate pilot reserve.
+- `art-brief.md`: architecture constraints and the focused first review scope.
+
+Official photo copies remain under the isolated `landmark-references/park-*`
+artifacts. The four generation inputs were the restored elevation, the actual
+wooden bridge, the accepted Station study and a native overworld screenshot.
+Two other official pavilion photographs were inspected as supporting references.
+
+The PNG was sent for its independent architecture review immediately after
+generation and copying. Other landmark and block-fill work does not wait for this
+metadata pack or get bundled into the same decision. This pack contains one
+first study, no native conversion and no commits.
