+# City v2: reusable native streetscape library
+
+This is the reusable map-fill workstream. It supplies source-compatible building
+and object modules while geography determines streets and the landmark stream
+develops bespoke art. No current maps, native map IDs, landmark doors, tileset
+headers, gameplay scripts or ROM outputs are changed by this library.
+
+The source catalog is `data/taichung/prefabs/catalog.json`, schema version1.
+Its seventeen implemented modules use existing General/PewterCity metatiles as
+temporary visuals. They are **not finished Taiwanese streetscape art**. Their
+purpose is to establish reusable dimensions, safe collision and placement rules,
+and stable asset/category IDs that geography can consume immediately.
+
+## Native modules
+
+Dimensions below include the final one-row clear apron.
+
+| Stable prefab ID | Size | Category |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `building-rowhouse-compact` | 5×5 | residential-lowrise |
+| `building-rowhouse-pair` | 10×5 | residential-lowrise |
+| `building-corner-store` | 5×5 | commercial-frontage |
+| `building-shopfront-wide` | 7×6 | commercial-frontage |
+| `building-walkup-low` | 5×6 | residential-walkup |
+| `building-walkup-tall` | 5×8 | residential-walkup |
+| `building-service-hall` | 11×8 | civic-service |
+| `building-kiosk-glass` | 4×5 | neighborhood-service |
+| `stall-market-red` | 4×4 | market-stall |
+| `prop-sign-board` | 1×2 | street-furniture |
+| `prop-shrub` | 1×2 | planting |
+| `prop-flower-bed` | 3×2 | planting |
+| `prop-tree-wide` | 2×3 | planting |
+| `prop-tree-line` | 4×3 | planting |
+| `prop-park-gateway` | 5×3 | park-edge |
+| `prop-low-brick-edge` | 4×2 | park-edge |
+| `ground-paving-pad` | 4×3 | ground-surface |
+
+The source gym shell used for the wide shop has both the GYM lettering and central
+emblem removed. The civic hall remains visibly museum-derived. Repeated window
+bands form walk-up blockouts, not accurate Taiwanese architecture. These visuals
+can be replaced later while retaining agreed footprints and entrance anchors.
+
+Parked scooters, YouBike racks, bus shelters, benches and traffic lights are
+explicit `requires-custom-native-art` category reservations. They have no native
+words or implemented visual asset yet and cannot be placed by the compositor.
+
+## Schema and placement semantics
+
+Each implemented module contains:
+
+- A stable ID, role/category, allowed contexts/ground, provisional-art status,
+  material descriptor and source rectangle/construction provenance.
+- Zero-based native16×16 metatile coordinates, width/height and explicit native
+  map words. The patch anchor is its upper-left corner.
+- Three per-cell binary masks: `paint`, `solid` and `mandatoryClear`. All visible
+  building/roof cells are solid at elevation0, independent of story flags. The
+  park opening and surface modules retain explicitly clear elevation3 passages.
+- A final mandatory-clear apron row. Its native paving in the catalog is a visual
+  reference; its `paint` mask is zero, so real placement preserves destination
+  ground. Entrances protect the cell immediately south.
+- Optional named dormant entrance reservations, each with a façade word, active
+  native door word and southern approach. The catalog itself contains no active
+  door/warp behaviors. A reservation does not imply an enterable room.
+
+The compositor rejects solids placed on protected roads, previously reserved
+aprons/passages, water, blocked ground, incorrect elevations or another module.
+Only the declared mowed-grass and paving ground classes may be replaced; wild
+tall-grass habitat cannot silently become a building. Optional placement context
+tags are checked against the asset's allowed contexts.
+It returns a fresh word grid, leaving the caller's original grid unchanged if an
+error occurs. Painted modules cannot overlap each other. Aprons can share clear
+ground but cannot be covered by another building.
+
+`requires.primary` is General. Modules containing secondary metatiles additionally
+require PewterCity; modules using only primary graphics work with other compatible
+General secondary banks. Metadata declares the current native640 primary /384
+secondary graphic-tile capacity and thirteen active background palettes (primary
+indices0–6; secondary7–12). Source files currently use640/288 graphic tiles.
+
+Measured catalog union:131 primary and69 secondary8×8 graphics, with secondary
+palette banks8,9,10,11. Secondary source graphic indices range up to111, so112
+source slots cover the selected graphics without repacking; unused metatile
+definitions would still need cleanup in a new bank. `validation.json` includes
+the exact secondary source-index list and per-module counts. Combining a repacked
+69-tile kit with the Station's tentative224-tile target would use293/384 graphics.
+Palette banks7 and12 are unused by this catalog and could be considered for that
+two-palette Station target. These are measured/proposed budgets only: no source
+graphics, palette banks, metatile definitions or approved allocation was changed.
+
+## Entrances and actual warps
+
+All entrance reservations render as solid dormant façade tiles by default.
+Activating one requires a placement `doors` binding and a `source_map` argument.
+The compositor reads registered native `map.json` files and checks:
+
+1. The exterior warp exists at the exact placed entrance coordinate.
+2. Its destination map and destination warp match the binding.
+3. The selected interior warp returns to that same exterior map/warp index.
+
+Only then is the dormant tile replaced with General0x03D, the native animated
+door, and a verified entrance record emitted. The library never registers maps or
+writes warp events. The map owner authors paired event data and later runs full
+world traversal validation, including all interior exit tiles.
+
+Example placement, still dormant:
+
+```json
+{"id":"shop-07","prefab":"building-corner-store","x":10,"y":20}
+```
+
+The `doors.front` binding shape is:
+
+```json
+{"warpIndex":0,"destMap":"MAP_EXISTING_REGISTERED_INTERIOR","destWarpId":1}
+```
+
+This shape alone cannot activate a door: the native source metadata must match.
+
+## Tools and reproduction
+
+`build_library.py` regenerates only this catalog from original source rectangles
+and named native tile components. `library.py` validates or composes modules;
+rendering uses the existing true-source metatile renderer and requires Pillow.
+Validation/composition and the regression checks otherwise use the standard library.
+
+```sh
+python3 tools/taichung/streetscape/build_library.py
+python3 tools/taichung/streetscape/library.py validate
+python3 tools/taichung/streetscape/check_library.py
+
+/Users/peter/.pyenv/versions/3.11.15/bin/python3 \
+  tools/taichung/streetscape/library.py catalog \
+  --output /Users/peter/devday_hackathon/artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/streetscape/prefab-catalog.png
+
+/Users/peter/.pyenv/versions/3.11.15/bin/python3 \
+  tools/taichung/streetscape/library.py compose \
+  --placements data/taichung/prefabs/example-block.json \
+  --output /Users/peter/devday_hackathon/artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/streetscape/example-block
+```
+
+The composition fixture is an unregistered64×48 source layout demonstrating
+ordinary blocks, a market plaza, protected avenues and a park opening. Its
+`map.bin` is a native-word fixture, not an installed or playable city area. All
+doors remain dormant. It produces358 solid cells,784 protected clear cells and
+a deterministic SHA-256 recorded in its manifest; no existing game grid is changed.
+
+## Validation and review artifacts
+
+Catalog validation covers defined metatile IDs, every referenced native8×8 graphic,
+the active palette range, mask/word agreement, clear elevation3 approaches, solid
+roof/building footprints, dormant-door safety and unavailable-art reservations.
+Eleven regression checks pass, exercising protected streets, blocked/tree/water
+aprons, overlapping modules, atomic composition, unbound doors, real paired native
+door activation, deliberate broken returns, out-of-bounds placements, bad palettes
+and accidental active warp behaviors in a dormant catalog.
+
+Artifacts under `artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/streetscape/`:
+
+- `prefab-catalog.png`: source-rendered module library, with orange dormant entrance
+  reservations and green apron markers.
+- `validation.json`: per-asset native dimensions, palettes and graphic usage.
+- `example-block/source-preview.png`: source-only composition fixture.
+- `example-block/map.bin` and `manifest.json`: reproducible native-word fixture and
+  entrance reservations.
+
+These source-rendered examples were visually inspected. They establish technical
+reuse and placement safety; Taiwan-specific skins remain the next art step.
