+# Parallel city expansion workstreams
+
+The user approved three parallel streams on 7 November 2026: the real city shape
+and streets, a library of ordinary buildings/physical objects for map fill, and
+bespoke landmark customization beginning with the most important places. The ten
+selected landmarks remain the gyms. Ordinary neighborhoods fill the city around
+them; they do not automatically become additional gyms.
+
+The current native city at `f099c12` remains the working integration baseline.
+These streams prepare independent inputs for the next map pass. Their first
+review pack is a sourced street/region draft, a reusable prefab catalog, and one
+Old Station art study. A rendered draft or generated image is not by itself a
+playable native map change.
+
+## Ownership
+
+| Stream | First concrete output | Owned files | Excludes |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Geography | Real major-road/rail/water geometry; neighborhood classifications; section/connection draft | `tools/taichung/geography/`, `docs/city-v2-geography.md`, `docs/city-v2-streets.json` | Existing map grids, warp/startup changes, tileset registration |
+| Streetscape library | Named ordinary-building and prop modules; placement/collision/entrance metadata; source-rendered catalog | `tools/taichung/streetscape/`, `data/taichung/prefabs/`, `docs/city-v2-streetscape.md` | Actual map placement, game-event warps, bespoke landmark art |
+| Landmark art | Official reference/specification and one photo-referenced Old Station pixel-art study | `data/taichung/landmarks/old-station/`, `docs/city-v2-landmark-art.md`; isolated reference/art artifacts | Other landmarks' production art, existing map edits, global asset registration |
+| Mapping integration | Shared contracts, native tile registration, composed grids, connections, collision and arrivals, integration checks | Existing native map/layout/tileset registries, this coordination document | Main's menus, battle/progression state, language implementation, release publication |
+
+All work stays in `.worktrees/game-mapping`. Agents write disjoint leaf paths;
+the mapping integrator reviews and commits their outputs serially. Main remains
+the sole owner of the canonical ROM, assembled release and publication. Gameplay
+and localization continue independently against the existing native interface.
+
+The first review pack is now prepared: a16-section municipal-road draft with102
+unpainted candidate lots, a17-module source-prefab catalog, and one recognizable
+Old Station study. Geography contract checks and eleven native-prefab fault checks
+pass. The cross-stream adapter finds at least one compatible lot for every module
+and rejects unknown contexts or undersized reserves. No existing map grid, door,
+startup flow, native tileset or ROM was changed by this preparation pack.
+
+Review artifacts under `artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/`:
+
+- `geography/city-v2-street-draft.png`: sourced street/section/reserve overlay.
+- `streetscape/prefab-catalog.png`: the reusable source-native module library.
+- `streetscape/example-block/source-preview.png`: unregistered composition fixture.
+- `streetscape/geography-fill-options.json`: compatible module/context options.
+- `landmark-art/old-station-study-v1.png`: photo-referenced generated art study.
+
+The next native composition pass resolves the four gym-envelope conflicts,
+simplifies the selected road network, supplies the missing rail/water constraints,
+and paints chosen modules into authored sections. Native art conversion and the
+versioned map/door/save interface are integrated deliberately after those inputs.
+
+## Shared coordinate and asset contracts
+
+The basic placement unit is one 16×16-pixel metatile. Graphics use 8×8 tiles.
+Dimensions must state whether they include the mandatory clear approach/apron.
+All module origins and entrances are zero-based local coordinates.
+
+The geography draft uses a provisional 256×256 world, divided into sixteen
+64×64 sections, over the central urban source bounds longitude120.62–120.72,
+latitude24.11–24.20. This is an engineering sizing assumption, approximately eight
+times the current outdoor tile area, rather than a finalized city placement.
+
+Real WGS84 geometry, raw projected positions, and authored game positions remain
+separate fields. A uniform projection puts some landmarks too close together to
+fit their artwork. The placement pass must reserve their footprints and locally
+adjust streets/distances while preserving recognizable geographic relationships.
+The source centerlines remain available to assess those adjustments.
+
+Geography supplies roads and block/land-use roles. The fill pass selects named
+modules by role and district context, without embedding tile IDs in the geographic
+data. Prefabs supply:
+
+- A stable ID, category, compatible tileset, and source/art status.
+- Exact width/height and native metatile words for provisional source modules.
+- A blocked building/prop footprint and a separate mandatory-clear path/apron mask.
+- Door reservations, facing, and clear southern approach where appropriate.
+- Placement context/material tags and rules for later visual replacements.
+
+A reserved door is activated only when the map integrator creates a valid paired
+warp. Non-enterable facades contain no active animated warp-door behavior.
+Buildings, NPCs and props may not occupy road/arrival/approach reservations.
+Actual gym entrances, return IDs, safe transport arrivals and save migration are
+published together by the mapping integrator before the expanded grids replace
+the baseline.
+
+The current prefab preview uses General + Pewter City tiles, explicitly labeled
+as provisional reused art. A later Taiwanese streetscape skin can replace their
+visuals while retaining useful footprints. Planned categories without real native
+art, such as scooters or YouBike docks, remain marked as reserved rather than
+being shown as completed assets.
+
+## Landmark priority and first art envelope
+
+Old Station comes first because it is the selected starting point and is visible
+immediately. The study follows official building photographs: red brick, cream
+stone bands, charcoal/slate hipped roofs, a central clock tower, an arched window
+and the low entrance canopy. The physical station roof must not inherit the
+prototype museum's pink roof merely because the prototype is a style reference.
+
+The initial art envelope is 12×8 metatiles (192×128 logical pixels), with an
+entry spanning columns5–6 of the bottom row. The right entry cell reserves the
+existing door at local(6,7), matching global(32,64) if placed at(26,57). The
+southern approach remains global(32,65); safe arrival stays(30,66). This envelope
+fits within the current exterior without changing the accepted startup position.
+Its enlarged image-study output is not a substitute for native indexed/tile data.
+
+The first study establishes silhouette, proportions, pixel density and material
+colors. Native use additionally requires indexed palette control, tile packing,
+collision/door metadata, a compatible tileset and actual game inspection. The
+geography and ordinary-building work do not wait for this art to be finished.
+Further landmark production follows review of this first result.
+
+## First cross-stream graphics budget
+
+The initial source-prefab catalog measures 69 referenced secondary 8×8 graphics
+and four secondary palette banks (8–11). It also references 131 graphics already
+in the shared General primary bank. The source Pewter image contains more tiles
+than this catalog uses; retaining every unused source graphic is unnecessary for
+a future combined city tileset.
+
+The Station specification targets at most224 new graphics and two palette banks.
+A repacked69+224 combination would use293 of384 secondary graphics, leaving91.
+Keeping the referenced source prefix of112 graphics instead would use336 and
+leave48. Palette banks7 and12 are a possible fit alongside the existing kit's
+four banks, subject to actual indexed-art validation and central allocation.
+These are measured source usage plus a proposed Station budget, not a completed
+native asset bank. Existing General/Pewter tiles and palettes remain unchanged.
+
+The generated Station study has the requested dimensions and recognizable
+architecture, but fails exact pixel-grid/palette/alpha requirements. Its metadata
+therefore keeps `nativeReady=false`. Native conversion and a combined-bank check
+must happen before any map starts consuming it.
+
+## Connecting the geography and fill streams
+
+`data/taichung/prefabs/geography-bindings.json` explicitly maps geographic fill
+roles/recipe names onto the catalog's categories and allowed placement contexts.
+For example, an authored `mixed-residential-retail` section can consider the kit's
+`mixed-use`, `residential` and `shopping` contexts. These aliases are design choices,
+not a claim about real zoning.
+
+The street draft offers12×8 lot reserves where clear and8×8 fallbacks. The wider
+option matters because the paired rowhouse and service hall are10 and11 tiles
+wide. Actual module dimensions already include their required apron space.
+
+Run the cross-stream sizing/context check with:
+
+```sh
+python3 -B tools/taichung/streetscape/plan_fill.py \
+  --output /Users/peter/devday_hackathon/artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/streetscape/geography-fill-options.json
+```
+
+It reports compatible module/context options per candidate lot and records input
+hashes. It rejects unknown recipes/roles or lots that cannot fit any building. It
+assigns no prefab, activates no door and paints no native map. Final composition
+still applies the native library's masks to authored roads, water, gym envelopes
+and other placed modules.
+
+The real road extract is a source layer for authoring. Parallel carriageways,
+minor branches and dense intersections need simplification before becoming game
+streets. All selected source lines must not automatically become wide paved game
+corridors. Landmark clearance and the balance of streets/buildings/parks are
+reviewed together before the next native grid is written.
+
+## First-review acceptance
+
+Geography must identify its source, fetch time and bounds; retain real source
+geometry; expose section crossings/road hierarchy; and show any footprint conflicts
+or missing data. Invented street traces must not be presented as real city data.
+
+The prefab catalog must render from actual source words and reject undefined tiles,
+incompatible tilesets, blocked door approaches and unintended active doors. It must
+be useful for denser neighborhoods even while the art remains provisional.
+
+The Station study must resemble the actual building without relying on a label,
+use the game-facing perspective, preserve the entrance concept, and state which
+native conversion checks remain. Only one landmark receives a production study
+at this stage.
+
+Integration checks come after the inputs are composed: native map-buffer capacity,
+connected walking/cycling paths, collisions, entrances/returns, transport arrivals,
+and native build/runtime tests. New-game, old saves, ten-gym progress, localization
+and the visitor guide require the corresponding versioned placement contract with
+Main. No worker independently rewrites the shared baseline generator or current
+map contract while those interfaces are being prepared.
