+# Graphical starter selector — source candidate
+
+This is a native-ROM presentation candidate for the requested short opening.
+It uses existing FireRed Pokémon graphics, with a selected 64×64 front portrait
+on the left and four animated party icons/names on the right. Blue header,
+selection and instruction panels fit the 240×160 GBA display. The selected
+partner's type and the shared ready-to-use level are visible. This visual
+direction needs a real emulator screenshot for review; it is not final art.
+
+The preserved order is Charmander, Bulbasaur, Squirtle, Pikachu. Left/Up moves
+back and Right/Down moves forward with wrapping. A opens confirmation. B from
+confirmation returns to the same preview. A second A confirms. B at initial
+selection cannot exit without a partner.
+
+## Native boundary
+
+`ShowTaichungStarterMenu(MainCallback returnCallback)` sets `VAR_RESULT` to
+`SPECIES_NONE`, opens the screen, then returns a confirmed species through
+`VAR_RESULT`. It never writes a party, starter marker, map, save variable or
+badge. `TaichungStarter_ScriptOpenMenu` performs the ordinary field-window
+cleanup and supplies `CB2_ReturnToFieldContinueScriptPlayMapMusic`; call it
+from the opening script with `callnative` followed by `waitstate`.
+
+The caller owns validation, the idempotent one-time real grant and the later
+outdoor warp. If the native window allocation fails, the menu returns
+`SPECIES_NONE` so the caller must reopen selection. A failed large-portrait
+allocation leaves the four small icons/names usable, with a text fallback in
+the portrait panel. No failed visual allocation chooses a Pokémon.
+
+The screen releases the portrait's native image allocation on each species
+switch and on exit, destroys its four icon sprites, frees icon palettes and
+the full-screen window buffer, then invokes the return callback. Static state
+uses twelve bytes before alignment: callback, portrait ID, four icon IDs,
+selection index and confirmation flag. The portrait uses OBJ palette eight;
+the icon palettes use their native tagged slots, avoiding palette overlap.
+
+## Text and review scope
+
+UI instructions and the four starter names follow the current native language
+preference. Chinese lines are no longer than thirteen glyphs; the longest is
+156 pixels at the current twelve-pixel advance. The new source needs exactly
+`毒水電` beyond the current charmap. Main/localization must regenerate the
+existing shared glyph union; this module does not alter the renderer.
+
+These short UI labels are presentation placeholders. Story owns the welcome,
+speaker, selection dialogue and confirmation prose. Main owns startup-hook
+integration and Landmarks owns the room/anchors. This source candidate does
+not claim that the new indoor opening, one-time grant, outdoor transition,
+Save/Continue acceptance or all-four runtime checks have already shipped.
