+# National Taichung Theater native installation
+
+This increment installs the approved Theater facade in Xitun against released
+native source `d7053fd115b3744b22a2ba3160b4240f5cc80355`. Its entrance remains
+`(12,44)`, approach `(12,45)`, arrival `(12,47)` and exterior warp 2. The existing
+room, host, gym ID, three return records and every other landmark anchor remain
+unchanged. No neighborhood fill, gameplay, save, startup or character changes are
+included. The presentation ROM and presenter save are separate preserved artifacts.
+
+Only Xitun's secondary tileset changes. All three connected exteriors retain
+`gTileset_TaichungOldCorePrimary`, because camera transitions reload secondary
+graphics only. Xitun uses `gTileset_TaichungXitun`: 337 unique graphics, 352 loaded
+slots and 239 metatile definitions. Graphics 1016–1023 remain available to door
+animation. The Theater uses palette 7; source palettes 8–11 remain intact.
+
+The exact borrowed Xitun/Greenway strips contain protected General metatiles only:
+Xitun sees Greenway x0–7/y0–38; Greenway sees Xitun x33–39/y25–63. All 1,530 borrowed
+cells across the entire three-district graph retain identical RGB and attributes.
+The original Old City and Greenway grids/banks remain unchanged. The Theater's
+first three transparent rows retain all 81 Maple street cells. The front art row
+uses COVERED layering; the roof uses NORMAL layering. The existing animated
+General door intentionally replaces one painted entrance cell.
+
+`install_theater.py --install` checks the released interfaces, unchanged context
+and exact border rendering before serial registration. `check_theater.py` checks
+art encoding, all 40,960 candidate pixels, palettes, source metatiles, collision,
+Maple paths and deterministic conversion. `check_old_core.py --self-test` retains
+the Old City protection checks and allows only this checked Xitun bank exception.
+`validate_city.py --baseline d7053fd --json` checks all ten gyms and connections.
+
+The shared gym's three return records remain at `(5,14)`, `(6,14)` and `(7,14)`.
+Only the center record has the original south-arrow warp behavior. The side
+records are walkable landing metadata, not three independent animated exits.
+Runtime evidence must distinguish side approach coverage from the center trigger.
+
+`data/taichung/landmarks/theater/native-delta.json` compares exact released Git
+source with registered Xitun. There are 109 changed map words and 33 newly blocked
+formerly walkable coordinates. Each has a verified connected fallback at most
+three tiles away. All 1,516 currently valid coordinates retain their saved
+position. Main owns the next save-version migration and cached-view reload;
+this source increment does not implement or claim old-version-3 compatibility.
+Current-candidate Save/Continue evidence is not old-cache migration evidence.
+
+The minimap's IDs, dimensions, world origins and landmark anchors are unchanged.
+Its source hash is refreshed; geometry fingerprint remains
+`924380bc2dfe7176686fd81395a52b8489ff18ff6401442acdf06a5d41331722`.
+That identity does not imply collision or cached-view compatibility.
+
+Build and runtime artifacts stay under
+`artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/theater-native/`. Main receives a clean source
+checkpoint, exact-ROM hashes, native screenshots and a delta read from that
+immutable checkpoint. Main alone integrates save migration and publishes.
