+# Fengjia and Maple Garden native increment
+
+This source increment installs the final two approved landmark exteriors. All ten planned landmarks now have distinct source artwork. It is separate from the frozen CMPc1 and Miyahara961 test cartridges; in-game acceptance and Main-owned publication remain pending.
+
+Fengjia's rainbow sign, four yellow stars and round end panels frame a single gym portal. The native door stays24,12, with approach24,13 and arrival24,15. Its dark lane is solid landmark art except for the one General door cell, not a traversable market street. The160×96 art begins19,7 and uses palette9.
+
+Maple Garden's pond, planted banks, winding paths and smaller modern pavilion begin10,27 in a160×112 envelope. The authored7×10 terrain mask gives49 passable cells and21 solid/door cells. Pond core, pavilion mass and steep/tree barriers block movement; paths, open grass, viewing deck and bridge landings use the reviewed coarse native foot plane. The source raster remains unchanged. The General door12,32 replaces local2,5 and the original paved approach12,33 replaces local2,6, producing a clear south landing. Arrival12,35 and the distinct south park stairs remain connected. Both raster templates remain in the bank for format fidelity, including the unused approach template.
+
+The Xitun primary preserves all228 General raw graphic slots, including70 animation destinations. It holds336 relocated legacy patterns and76 new-art patterns; the secondary uses282 static graphics, padded to288 loaded tiles. All239 old secondary metatile IDs/renderings/attributes remain compatible, including all Theater art. Exact legacy palette8/9 colors move to unused10/11 and only those references are remapped; new Maple/Fengjia use8/9. Theater7 and roof palette12 remain unchanged. The total351 definitions leave33 available; door scratch1016–1023 remains unused.
+
+The immutable source pack remains in `taichung_xitun_final`; actual registered graphics/palettes plus composed definitions live in the separate `taichung_xitun_landmarks` secondary. The primary is `taichung_xitun_private`. The compiled final-scene inputs remain unregistered proposal artifacts with separate `installation.json` attesting the actual C/layout/map registration. Do not overwrite the pack's templates when rebuilding an installed scene.
+
+```
+python3 -B tools/taichung/landmarks/check_xitun_final.py --self-test
+python3 -B tools/taichung/landmarks/check_cmp.py --self-test
+python3 -B tools/taichung/streetscape/check_miyahara_area.py --self-test --json
+python3 -B tools/taichung/landmarks/check_old_core.py --self-test --json
+python3 -B tools/taichung/export_minimap.py --check
+```
+
+The new independent guard reconstructs181 changed words from exact Git source, approved PNG pixels and the pinned semantic mask. It verifies loaded C fields, palette paths, General callback, all legacy RGB/attributes, protected raw slots, candidate foregrounds, masks and all1,530 donor cells' exact raw entries/RGB/attributes. All ten gym approaches and thirty interior returns pass source geometry. Eight corruption probes are rejected. CMP's cohort guard permits this one named bank pair only through that independent reconstruction, alongside the separately guarded Miyahara area.
+
+Compared with the unchanged e9/c1/961 Xitun geometry,29 formerly ordinary positions become blocked and85 open, leaving1572 ordinary positions. All nine Xitun door/approach/arrival words remain exact. Safe fallback candidates and the full coordinate delta are recorded in the final-scene manifest; Main must independently attest the integrated source and allocate subsequent cache/version handling. The prior Theater migration and CMP/Miyahara migrations still apply to older saves.
+
+Source proofs do not establish asynchronous primary-upload behavior or live movement. Native acceptance must include both new doors, Maple's playable paths, preserved Theater, normal walking/cycling across each changed bank boundary, layering, save/reset/Continue and the combined client. Keep the live release and frozen earlier test ROMs separate until those gates pass. Canonical source, save code, exports and publication remain Main-owned.
